{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said.</b> This is the response to \"And how will Pharaoh hear me, when I am of uncircumcised lips?\" HaShem answered him: \"See, I have set you as Elohim to Pharaoh.\"" "\"And He said\": the meaning of \"See\" — I have made for you a great elevation, that you will be accounted in Pharaoh's eyes like the elevation of an angel, and this is \"Elohim.\" And He speaks to the prophet, and the prophet speaks to the people of his generation." "Those who say that נביא is derived from \"ניב שפתים\" (Isaiah 57:19) are incorrect, for the root of ניב is of the two-letter class, according to the opinion of the sages of France and those who follow the eye [i.e., grammarians who judge by visual analogy], while according to the sages of Spain [it is] of the three-letter class, and the root of נביא is three letters. The proof: \"נביאים\" (Numbers 11:29), \"ויתנבאו\" (ibid. 11:25) — for the alef is a root letter. Furthermore, \"ניב שפתים\" is like \"fruit,\" for it is derived from \"תנובה\" (Isaiah 27:6), \"עוד ינובון בשיבה\" (Psalms 92:15), and trustworthy proof: \"ניבו נבזה אכלו\" (Malachi 1:12). And furthermore: what is the meaning of \"Restore the man's wife, for he is a נביא\" (Genesis 20:7)? If its meaning were \"speaker,\" that would be nothing; rather, its meaning is: he is a נביא, to whom I reveal My secrets, in the manner of \"Surely HaShem does nothing without revealing His secret to His servants the prophets\" (Amos 3:7). And he takes pleasure in Me; therefore \"ויתפלל בעדך וחיה\" (Genesis 20:7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "The clause והוא מתענג עלי ע\"כ is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax and reference are compressed and the text may be subtly corrupt, but no smoothing has been applied."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:22.562729524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}